  "custom_logic_notes": "Composite scoring system: 5 SMAs per timeframe compared current vs previous bar to determine up/down direction (1/0 each). AC indicator contributes 0 or 3 per timeframe based on complex momentum/divergence pattern. Max raw score = 5 (SMA) + 3 (AC) = 8 per timeframe. Multiplied by 12.5 gives 0-100% per timeframe. Signal requires ALL 3 timeframes to agree: >50% for weak signal (1/-1), >=75% for strong signal (2/-2). OpenLevel/CloseLevel inputs gate which signal strength triggers opens/closes. Entry blocked if opposite close signal also active (e.g. OpenBuy requires !OpenSell && !CloseBuy). AC scoring logic: +3 up if (3-bar declining AC turns up while negative) OR (3-bar rising AC while positive); +3 down if inverse; 0 if mixed/neutral. TF2 (H1) AC is NOT used (u2acv/d2acv are never assigned - remains 0). Trailing stop only activates when price has moved Trailing pips beyond entry, ensuring breakeven-plus before trailing engages.",
