  "python_conversion_notes": "Multi-timeframe SMA comparison is straightforward. The AC oscillator is standard (Bill Williams) and available in most Python TA libraries (e.g. ta-lib ACOSCALES). Key complexity: the AC scoring logic uses a multi-bar pattern (4 bars: Shift, Shift+1, Shift+2, Shift+3) with conditional branching for 3 possible states (bullish=3, bearish=3, neutral=0). This must be implemented exactly as coded. Note bug/quirk: u2acv and d2acv are declared but never assigned values in the Indicators() function, so TF2 AC contribution is always 0 - this may be intentional or a bug in the original. The Signal integer (-2,-1,0,1,2) threshold logic with OpenLevel/CloseLevel inputs must be preserved. Trailing stop logic checks StopsLevel minimum distance. Position gate is strict: only one position at a time per symbol.",
